00:32:48.130 --> 00:32:48.490
Come on.

00:32:49.470 --> 00:32:50.370
I didn't hurt you.

00:32:50.650 --> 00:32:54.000
It was never that kind of thing.

00:32:54.980 --> 00:32:58.140
I remember you scratching my cornea really bad

00:32:58.140 --> 00:32:59.760
and bending my arm.

00:33:00.060 --> 00:33:01.560
In ways, it's not supposed to bend.

00:33:01.700 --> 00:33:02.480
You know what I mean.

00:33:03.220 --> 00:33:05.180
We were each other's in-between people, you know?

00:33:06.090 --> 00:33:07.330
You helped me get over Jody,

00:33:07.840 --> 00:33:10.480
and I helped you get over Summer.

00:33:16.180 --> 00:33:22.270
It's kind of cool, actually.

00:33:25.530 --> 00:33:28.740
We helped get each other ready for what's next.

00:33:30.250 --> 00:33:30.870
Good luck with that.

00:33:31.010 --> 00:33:34.390
It was summer.

00:33:44.490 --> 00:33:46.020
Look at this!

00:33:46.180 --> 00:33:48.500
Well, I figured you could use a home-cooked meal.

00:33:48.950 --> 00:33:51.330
Grilled salmon and a raspberry coulis reduction.

00:33:51.550 --> 00:33:52.290
My favorite.

00:33:52.710 --> 00:33:52.930
No.

00:33:53.290 --> 00:33:54.090
My hero.

00:33:55.740 --> 00:33:57.300
You shaved.

00:33:57.620 --> 00:33:58.720
Well, I clean up nice.

00:34:00.860 --> 00:34:02.260
So, you've been working hard.

00:34:03.070 --> 00:34:04.090
It's a good thing you got the new office.

00:34:04.210 --> 00:34:04.690
How do you like it?

00:34:05.150 --> 00:34:08.110
Well, it's a little rough around the edges.

00:34:08.390 --> 00:34:09.350
It's just my style.

00:34:09.690 --> 00:34:11.170
Well, if you're going to be spending a lot of time there,

00:34:11.270 --> 00:34:12.170
you're going to need to spruce it up.

00:34:12.850 --> 00:34:13.930
I like it unspruced.

00:34:15.510 --> 00:34:17.770
Well, while you are whipping up a culinary miracle,

00:34:17.970 --> 00:34:19.890
I'm going to go to the store and pick up some things from my dad.

00:34:22.990 --> 00:34:23.390
I love you.

00:34:45.520 --> 00:34:53.660
Summer. So, I've been...

00:34:53.660 --> 00:34:54.360
Yeah, I've been thinking.

00:34:55.090 --> 00:34:55.610
Sorry, go.

00:34:55.770 --> 00:34:57.370
No, no, you go first.

00:34:57.680 --> 00:34:58.020
Yes, okay.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:06.580
Um, I'm not happy with the, uh, shadings of my sketches.

00:35:06.780 --> 00:35:10.280
I'm glad to hear that, because I've, um, made some modifications to my costume.

00:35:10.460 --> 00:35:10.860
Oh.

00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:12.420
And Princess Sparkle now has a cape.

00:35:12.520 --> 00:35:13.420
Nice touch. Fantastic.

00:35:14.100 --> 00:35:17.600
I always say, every four-legged sidekick, they need a cape.

00:35:17.740 --> 00:35:18.020
Yes.

00:35:18.260 --> 00:35:19.000
I always say that.

00:35:19.180 --> 00:35:20.410
Yeah, good.

00:35:22.030 --> 00:35:23.070
So do you need to draw me again?

00:35:23.190 --> 00:35:24.450
No, that's not necessary.

00:35:24.740 --> 00:35:25.740
That is not necessary.

00:35:25.740 --> 00:35:26.640
I've got your image.

00:35:26.720 --> 00:35:28.440
It's just seared in my memory.

00:35:29.380 --> 00:35:29.640
Good.

00:35:30.830 --> 00:35:33.410
I think, yeah. I look forward to seeing what you come up with.

00:35:34.630 --> 00:35:42.680
Here's the thing. I just think that the best way for us to maintain a professional relationship...

00:35:42.680 --> 00:35:44.440
Is to spend as little time together as possible.

00:35:44.620 --> 00:35:45.400
Yes, exactly.

00:35:45.940 --> 00:35:46.160
Good.

00:35:46.880 --> 00:35:48.200
Who's ready for a road trip?

00:35:48.380 --> 00:35:48.600
What?

00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:51.740
I just talked to the guy at Wildstorm. He loved your drawings.

00:35:52.020 --> 00:35:55.920
I set up a meeting. We're going to San Diego. Just the three of us.

00:35:59.270 --> 00:35:59.630
Great.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:08.370
I think about how it might happen.

00:36:31.310 --> 00:36:36.030
It's not that I don't understand you

00:36:36.030 --> 00:36:39.710
It's not that I don't miss you

00:36:39.710 --> 00:36:44.130
But you only want me the way you want

00:38:00.720 --> 00:38:18.600
Your fault.

00:38:30.670 --> 00:38:31.710
It's no one's fault.

00:38:36.130 --> 00:38:40.920
I think Caleb has changed, really.

00:38:41.420 --> 00:38:43.650
He wants a relationship with me.

00:38:46.800 --> 00:38:47.320
That's great.

00:38:50.070 --> 00:38:56.200
It's just, I think that that's gonna be pretty hard.

00:38:56.740 --> 00:38:57.480
Around, yeah.

00:38:58.690 --> 00:38:59.900
Look, I know.

00:39:00.950 --> 00:39:15.750
that he's gonna like you i mean that's gonna take some time it needs me now yeah we'll take

00:39:15.750 --> 00:39:20.160
some time off it's not like we haven't done it before i don't know it's first kirsten and now

00:39:20.160 --> 00:39:23.340
my dad yeah you don't want a relationship with julie cooper do you because i don't think we'd

00:39:23.340 --> 00:39:25.660
see each other yeah that's not gonna happen

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:36.100
It's like, you get it.

00:40:18.910 --> 00:40:20.990
It's me. I'm just checking up on you, making sure you're okay.

00:40:22.310 --> 00:40:24.800
I was just getting ready to sack out on the couch.

00:40:25.360 --> 00:40:27.440
All right. I'll see you in the morning.

00:40:28.890 --> 00:40:29.510
Figure this out.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:32.400
You leading the charge, I have no doubt.

00:40:34.130 --> 00:40:34.470
Good night.

00:40:35.770 --> 00:40:36.050
Good night.

00:40:37.020 --> 00:40:37.440
Thank you.

00:41:20.570 --> 00:41:21.190
Hey, sweetie, it's Mom.

00:41:21.770 --> 00:41:22.860
Hey, how's Grandpa?

00:41:23.750 --> 00:41:24.270
He's okay.

00:41:24.410 --> 00:41:24.850
I just saw him.

00:41:24.890 --> 00:41:25.530
Is your dad around?

00:41:27.570 --> 00:41:28.430
Hang on, let me check.

00:41:31.020 --> 00:41:36.090
Dad? I have no idea where he is right now.

00:41:36.490 --> 00:41:38.330
Okay, well, I'm going to make a pit stop.

00:41:38.530 --> 00:41:40.190
I'm going to drop a few things off at his office.

00:41:40.470 --> 00:41:41.550
Need some sprucing up.

00:41:42.370 --> 00:41:43.430
Did you say sprucing?

00:41:43.860 --> 00:41:44.860
Yes, I did indeed.

00:41:45.690 --> 00:41:48.850
All right. Listen, if he and I should cross paths,

00:41:48.950 --> 00:41:50.110
is there anything you want me to tell him?

00:41:50.650 --> 00:41:52.430
Nah, I want it to be a surprise.

00:41:52.750 --> 00:41:54.970
Just let him know that I'll be home in a few minutes.

00:41:55.350 --> 00:41:56.910
All right, I can do that. Bye-bye.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:00.160
Yeah.

00:42:02.360 --> 00:42:05.070
Hey, Ryan and I could use a little help set on the table.

00:42:05.770 --> 00:42:06.010
All right.

00:42:07.230 --> 00:42:07.550
Who called?

00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:08.920
Oh, his mom.

00:42:09.510 --> 00:42:09.770
Oh, yeah.

00:42:09.910 --> 00:42:10.430
What did she say?

00:42:10.690 --> 00:42:11.870
She's going to be home in a few.

00:42:31.060 --> 00:42:31.120
Thank you.
